 "researcher_notes": "Targa announced in August 2026 a new 70 mile residue gas pipeline called Bull Run II, added to its Bull Run residue system, to carry gas from three planned Delaware basin plants (Wrangler, Ranger, Ranger II, about 825 million cubic feet per day combined) to the Waha Hub. It is backed by take-or-pay commitments tied to new 20 year agreements with ExxonMobil, and the start date is the first half of 2028. Targa also raised its 2026 growth capital to about 5 billion dollars. Pipeline and Gas Journal, Oil and Gas Journal and the company release all trace to the same Targa announcement, so they count as one origin. Diameter, capacity and start point are not stated; the start is the new Delaware plants, not yet named in a source. It is a different line from P7854 Bull Run Extension (43 miles, under construction) and from P7852 Bull Run Gas Pipeline. Length 70 miles meets the 15.5 mile threshold. Texas Railroad Commission T-4 permit not checked. Owner spelling from the ownership gazetteer stem match (Targa Resources Corp); confirm. Route not researched; no route available."
